  base and head sites) are not always mixed: in
  GD-2's same-side family, at one of the doubled
  column's two sites the neighbour's factor can align
  with both copies, giving an all-plain or
  all-conjugated triple - the average of
  rho x rho x rho (resp. its conjugate), whose
  invariant space is the trivial-representation
  multiplicity in rho^{tensor 3}, a second
  per-representation number that no module in the
  tree owns in any form. (Recorded as this brick's
  analysis of the owned `siteKind` table applied to
  GD-2's landed three-factor seam; not a proved
  theorem of this module.)

- **(iii) The scope strand.** TW-1's evaluations are
  proved for FINITE `G` by finite averaging (its
